   "text": "The pattern matches **mp-1303315 (Mg2VWO6)** on its own. Confidence is moderate, about 0.7, because I matched peaks by position and did not simulate intensities.\n\n**Observed peaks.** I read these maxima from the grid:\n- Strongest: 23.85\u00b0 (100) and 33.05\u00b0 (67).\n- A doublet at about 35.1\u00b0 and 35.5\u00b0 (about 25 each).\n- Smaller peaks at 18.97\u00b0 (29), 20.78\u00b0 (77), 28.25\u00b0 (23), about 38.95\u00b0 (21) and about 40.6\u00b0 (26).\n\n**Why Mg2VWO6 fits.**\n- The sequence 23.9\u00b0, 33.1\u00b0, 35.1\u201335.5\u00b0 and about 40.6\u00b0 is the typical corundum/ilmenite-type pattern, near the (012), (104), (110) and (113) positions of that family.\n- Mg2VWO6 has a metal-to-oxygen ratio of 2:3 (Mg4V2W2O12), which fits a distorted, cation-ordered ilmenite-type structure.\n- That ordering would explain the extra low-angle peaks at 18.97\u00b0 and 20.78\u00b0 as superstructure reflections. This is plausible but not checked by calculating intensities.\n\n**Why the other candidates are rejected.**\n- **Cubic double perovskites (Ba2HoReO6, Ba2TbSnO6, BaSrCeSnO6):** their strongest line, (220), would fall near 29\u201330\u00b0, which is empty. The 18.97/20.78\u00b0 pair also does not have the spacing ratio expected for (111)/(200).\n- **Monoclinic Sr2TmTaO6 and Sr2ErTaO6:** both would need a dominant peak near 30.5\u00b0, which is not observed.\n- **NaReO3 (cubic, a = 3.888 \u00c5):** its peaks would be at about 22.9\u00b0, 32.6\u00b0 and 40.1\u00b0, which do not line up with 23.85\u00b0 and 33.05\u00b0.\n- **K3(CuO2)2:** it would give a strong low-angle (002) line near 16.1\u00b0, which is absent.\n- **VO2:** this cell resembles the M2 rutile-derived form, whose strongest line should be near 27.4\u201327.8\u00b0. The pattern has only a weak feature at 27.8\u00b0 and a peak of 23 at 28.25\u00b0, so VO2 is at most a minor possibility. The 28.25\u00b0 peak may instead be another Mg2VWO6 reflection.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-1303315\"], \"confidence\": 0.7, \"note\": \"Peaks at 23.85, 33.05 and 35.1-35.5 deg match a distorted ilmenite-type pattern consistent with Mg2VWO6, while the perovskite, NaReO3, K3(CuO2)2 and VO2 candidates lack their key lines; VO2 as a minor second phase cannot be fully excluded.\"}",
